---
// Joe's sketchbook doodles down the empty side margins of wide screens, like notes in
// a notebook's margin. The page ships only this empty layer: src/scripts/margin-doodles.ts
// draws them in the browser, from 1600px wide (margins of at least 224px beside the
// 72rem column), so their paths live once in a cached script instead of in every
// page's HTML. Decorative.
---

<div
	class="margin-doodles pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 hidden overflow-hidden min-[1600px]:block"
	aria-hidden="true"
></div>

<script>
	// Its own chunk, fetched only where the doodles draw: phones and laptops never use it
	if (matchMedia('(min-width: 1600px)').matches) import('../scripts/margin-doodles');
</script>
